<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n78111" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρακατα-βολή</span></b> , ἡ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>money deposited in
			court</i> by claimants, and forfeited in case of failure, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				49.46
			</span></i>, Lexap. eund.<i><span class="en">
				43.16
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρακαταβολὴ καὶ
					παρακαταβάλλειν</span>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>the process in which such a deposit was required</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				8.32
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> generally,
				<i>court-deposit</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπειδὴ θᾶττον ἀνείλετο τὰς π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					37.41
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίκας καὶ γραφὰς ἄνευ -βολῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					20.2
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>